  "scope": "Uncompressed single-stream AVI movie export in the C++ core, installed C++ SDK, Python API and both Dear ImGui hosts. Gray8 or RGB24; one bounded cycle along Z/C/T with inclusive range/stride, forward/reverse/ping-pong and explicit FPS or supported calibrated time.",
  "behavior": "UI exports rendered 8-bit display colors while preserving source sample bits, calibration, history and workflow. No implicit conversion of scientific source samples in the core Dataset adapter. Typed drafts are validated completely and retained when malformed. Explicit overwrite, staged atomic publication, cancellation, source/display revision checks and memory/file preflight protect output.",
  "limits": "Classic RIFF AVI, dimensions 1..32767, finite FPS 0.001..1000 rounded to six decimals; default 1 GiB file and 512 MiB core working limit. UI uses the processing-memory cap plus conservative display reservation. One frame, padded row and fixed 16 KiB header/index allowance; no complete movie/index buffer. The caller owns the source Dataset and any frame-provider allocations.",
